---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CompressTool from '../components/CompressTool.astro';
const title = 'Compress Image to 20KB Online - Free | CompressImg';
const description = 'Compress JPG, PNG, and WebP images to 20KB or less for strict forms, passport photos, and tiny uploads.';
const faqItems = [
  {
    question: 'How to compress image to 20KB?',
    answer: 'Upload your image using the tool above, which is pre-set to 20KB. The tool reduces quality and, when needed, pixel dimensions until the result is at or below 20KB.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Will a 20KB image look good?',
    answer: 'At 20KB, some quality loss is inevitable, but for small display sizes such as form uploads, the image can remain recognizable. Smaller dimensions and simpler images produce the best results.'
  }
];
---
<Layout title={title} description={description} canonical="/compress-image-to-20kb" schemaType="WebApplication" faqItems={faqItems}>
      <section class="border-b border-white/10 py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <p class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-white/10 bg-white/5 px-3.5 py-1.5 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-stone-400">
        <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-accent-400"></span>
        Compress to 20KB
      </p>
      <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl font-semibold leading-[1.08] tracking-tightest text-stone-50 md:text-5xl">Compress image to <span class="text-accent-300">20KB</span> online - free</h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-[60ch] text-base leading-relaxed text-stone-400 md:text-lg">Reduce your image to 20KB or less. Perfect for strict form requirements, tiny avatars, and minimal storage use. Supports JPG, PNG, and WebP.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 -mt-2 mb-12">
    <CompressTool defaultTarget={20} showCustomTarget={true} />
  </section>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pb-20 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <h2 class="mb-5 text-base font-semibold tracking-tight text-stone-100">Other compression sizes</h2>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3">
      <a href="/compress-image-to-30kb" class="rounded-full border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.04] px-4 py-2 font-mono text-sm font-medium text-stone-400 transition duration-200 hover:border-accent-400 hover:text-accent-300 active:scale-[0.97]">Compress to 30KB</a>
      <a href="/compress-image-to-50kb" class="rounded-full border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.04] px-4 py-2 font-mono text-sm font-medium text-stone-400 transition duration-200 hover:border-accent-400 hover:text-accent-300 active:scale-[0.97]">Compress to 50KB</a>
      <a href="/compress-image-to-100kb" class="rounded-full border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.04] px-4 py-2 font-mono text-sm font-medium text-stone-400 transition duration-200 hover:border-accent-400 hover:text-accent-300 active:scale-[0.97]">Compress to 100KB</a>
      <a href="/compress-image-to-200kb" class="rounded-full border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.04] px-4 py-2 font-mono text-sm font-medium text-stone-400 transition duration-200 hover:border-accent-400 hover:text-accent-300 active:scale-[0.97]">Compress to 200KB</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-stone-100">Why Compress Images to 20KB?</h2>
    <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed text-stone-400">A 20KB file size is one of the strictest requirements you'll encounter for image uploads. Many government portals, examination forms, and official document submission systems require photographs to be under 20KB. This extremely small size limit is designed to minimize server storage costs and ensure fast processing of millions of applications. While 20KB is challenging for high-quality images, modern compression techniques make it possible to achieve recognizable and acceptable results for identification purposes.</p>
    <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed text-stone-400">Common scenarios requiring 20KB images include government job application forms, university admission portals, examination registration systems, and visa application websites. These systems are designed to handle massive volumes of submissions, and small file sizes are essential for their operation. Our compress image to 20KB tool is specifically optimized to achieve this challenging target while preserving as much visual information as possible.</p>
    <h2 class="mb-4 mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-stone-100">Tips for Best 20KB Compression Results</h2>
    <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed text-stone-400">Getting the best possible image quality at 20KB requires some strategy. First, ensure your original image has appropriate dimensions. For a 20KB target, images around 200x200 to 400x400 pixels work best. Very large images will show significant compression artifacts when squeezed to 20KB. Second, use simple backgrounds when possible - plain or gradient backgrounds compress much better than busy, detailed backgrounds. Third, good lighting on your subject helps maintain clarity even at high compression levels.</p>
    <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed text-stone-400">It's important to set realistic expectations: a 20KB image is never going to look as sharp as the original. However, for the intended purpose - usually small display sizes on forms and identification cards - the quality is perfectly adequate. Our tool uses intelligent quality adjustment to find the sweet spot where the image is as clear as possible while meeting the strict 20KB requirement.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="border-t border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2 class="mb-10 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-stone-900 md:text-3xl">Frequently Asked Questions - 20KB Compression</h2>
      <div class="divide-y divide-white/10 border-y border-white/10">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn flex w-full items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 text-left text-[15px] font-medium text-stone-100 transition-colors hover:text-accent-300">
            How to compress image to 20KB?
            <svg class="faq-icon h-4 w-4 flex-shrink-0 text-stone-500 transition-transform duration-300 ease-[cubic-bezier(0.32,0.72,0,1)]" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-content hidden pb-5">
            <p class="max-w-[65ch] text-sm leading-relaxed text-stone-400">Upload your image using the tool above, which is pre-set to 20KB. The tool reduces quality and, when needed, pixel dimensions until the result is at or below 20KB.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn flex w-full items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 text-left text-[15px] font-medium text-stone-100 transition-colors hover:text-accent-300">
            Will a 20KB image look good?
            <svg class="faq-icon h-4 w-4 flex-shrink-0 text-stone-500 transition-transform duration-300 ease-[cubic-bezier(0.32,0.72,0,1)]" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-content hidden pb-5">
            <p class="max-w-[65ch] text-sm leading-relaxed text-stone-400">At 20KB, some quality loss is inevitable, but for small display sizes such as form uploads, the image can remain recognizable. Smaller dimensions and simpler images produce the best results.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll('.faq-btn').forEach(btn => {
    btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const content = btn.nextElementSibling;
      const icon = btn.querySelector('.faq-icon');
      content.classList.toggle('hidden');
      icon.classList.toggle('rotate-180');
    });
  });
</script>
